SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Section 80\, Pharmacy Dispensing Fees: Final 
 Draft Rate and Comment Summary
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Section 80\, Pharmacy Dispensing Fees: Final Draft Rate
  and Comment Summary\nSection 80\, Pharmacy Dispensing Fees: Final Draft R
 ate and Comment Summary\nAug 27\, 2026\nThe\nfinal draft rates\nand a\nsum
 mary of all comments\nare available on the MaineCare Rate System Reform we
 bpage. The comment summary includes the Department’s responses\, with an
  explanation of whether and how feedback was incorporated into the final d
 raft rates.  MaineCare considered all public input received. We thank all
  those who contributed.\nBackground\nMaineCare\ninitiated\nthis rate deter
 mination in December of 2024.\nLater in December of 2024\, vendor Meyers &
  Stauffer surveyed Maine pharmacy providers on the cost of delivering serv
 ices.\nIn May of 2026\, we held a virtual public\nkickoff meeting\nfor int
 erested parties. We reviewed project goals\, the scope of work and present
 ed draft rates with rationale for public comment.\nFollowing the public pr
 esentation of draft rates\, we accepted written comments through the deadl
 ine of June 10\, 2026.\nThe new rates will now move through the legislativ
 ely mandated rulemaking process.\nYou may view all related notices and pre
 sented materials to date\, on the\nRate System Reform webpage\n.\nFor ques
 tions on this process\, please contact\nMargaret Blume\n\, MaineCare’s P
 roject Lead.\nThis notice is sent pursuant to\nRate Reform law\n.\nhttps:/
 /www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/section-80-pharmacy-d
 ispensing-fees-final-draft-rate-and-comment-summary-2026-08-27
