SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Attention Trading Partners: Training for New 
 MaineCare Partner Portal
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Attention Trading Partners: Training for New MaineCare 
 Partner Portal\nAttention Trading Partners: Training for New MaineCare Par
 tner Portal\nAug 25\, 2026\nWe have\npreviously shared\nthat a refreshed a
 nd upgraded MIHMS\, with a new “MaineCare Partner Portal\,” is coming 
 in October 2026. This will replace the current HealthPAS Online Portal. We
  are now inviting trading partners to\nregister for training starting\nSep
 tember 8\, 2026\nto help you prepare for the transition to the new portal.
  Trading partners include providers\, billing agents\, health plans\, clea
 ringhouses\, and business associates. Trading partners have an important r
 ole to play in supporting a smooth transition and uninterrupted access to 
 the portal after go-live.\nGainwell Technologies will be leading live virt
 ual instructor-led training sessions. These courses will provide the knowl
 edge and skills needed to navigate the new portal\, complete daily busines
 s functions\, and use new portal features. Training demonstrations\, mater
 ials\, and supporting resources will help participants prepare for a succe
 ssful transition.\nSteps you need to take to attend training\nReview the a
 vailable training topics listed below and identify the sessions that align
  with your role and responsibilities.\nUse the LMS registration (instructi
 ons below) to create an account\, access the training catalog\, and enroll
  in applicable sessions.\nContact Gainwell (instructions below) if you nee
 d assistance.\nRecorded sessions and other training materials will be avai
 lable in the LMS after training sessions for ongoing reference.\nMaineCare
  Partner Portal Training Sessions\nCourse Name\nDescription\nME - TPT - Mi
 grated Trading Partner Log In and Account Maintenance Training (ILC)\nLear
 n how to complete first-time login activities\, configure multi-factor aut
 hentication (MFA)\, manage user accounts and permissions\, perform account
  \nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-t
 rading-partners-training-new-mainecare-partner-portal-2026-08-25
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-
 trading-partners-training-new-mainecare-partner-portal-2026-08-25
